.TH SDL_CreateTray 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateTray \- Create an icon to be placed in the operating system\(aqs tray, or equivalent.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Tray * SDL_CreateTray(SDL_Surface *icon, const char *tooltip);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Many platforms advise not using a system tray unless persistence is a necessary feature\[char46] Avoid needlessly creating a tray icon, as the user may feel like it clutters their interface\[char46]
.PP
You should set the
.BR SDL_PROP_APP_METADATA_IDENTIFIER_STRING
property to ensure correct behaviour on some platforms like Linux\[char46]
.PP
Using tray icons require the video subsystem\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I icon
a surface to be used as icon\[char46] May be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I tooltip
a tooltip to be displayed when the mouse hovers the icon in UTF-8 encoding\[char46] Not supported on all platforms\[char46] May be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns The newly created system tray icon\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

